       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like a possible error.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the maximum daily dose.** The usual adult dosing is:\n- Starting dose: 5 mg once daily (2.5 mg for older, frail or hepatically impaired patients)\n- Maximum dose: 10 mg once daily\n\nA dose of 50 mg is in overdose range. It could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia and shock. It's a common slip to type 50 when 5.0 or 5 mg was meant.\n\nCould you confirm what you intended?\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth, once daily.** This is the standard starting dose and the most likely intended order.\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth, once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n3. Something else, such as a different drug or dose.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
