      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one, and I want to explain why.\n\nThere's no recognized clinical use for amlodipine 50 mg daily. It's 5 times the maximum dose, which is the amount seen in overdose cases that end up needing ICU care. Because amlodipine stays in the body for 30 to 50 hours, the effects of an overdose last for days and are hard to reverse. Confirming the order doesn't change that risk. Pharmacy would also likely stop it at verification unless there's a documented reason.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth, once daily** right now if either was what you meant.\n- **Enter a different drug** if amlodipine wasn't the one you intended. Some drugs are commonly dosed at 50 mg, like metoprolol or losartan, and they're easy to mix up.\n- If you really do mean 50 mg for a specific reason, please talk with the pharmacist or attending first. You can then enter the order yourself with that reason documented.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
